- For a PR, read its description and changed files (`gh pr view <n> --json title,body,files`) and the linked plan in `docs/plans/`.
<!-- kit:end -->
<!-- kit:if !module.openPr -->
- For a branch or PR, read its description and the linked plan in `docs/plans/`.
<!-- kit:end -->
<!-- kit:adapt: Say where committed Playwright E2E specs live in this repo and how they are named (for example e2e/<feature>.e2e.ts in playwright.config.ts), and that one-off exploratory specs go in the artifact folder and are deleted before finishing. -->
- In every Playwright spec, save full-page screenshots (`page.screenshot({ path: ..., fullPage: true })`) at the key states into `process.env.E2E_ARTIFACT_DIR`, numbered in order (`01-<state>.png`, `02-<state>.png`).

### 2. Run it

From the checkout root:

    node .agents/skills/e2e-verify/scripts/e2e-verify.mjs

Pass arguments to Playwright after `--`, for example one spec file:

    node .agents/skills/e2e-verify/scripts/e2e-verify.mjs -- <path to one spec>

<!-- kit:adapt: Give the one-time command that installs Playwright's browser in this repo (for example npx playwright install chromium), and any machine-specific note (WSL libraries, an nvm Node version). -->

### 3. Review the screenshots

After `e2e-verify: PASS`, open **every** listed screenshot with your multimodal file-reading tool (`Read` / `view_file`) on a frontier model (`Opus` / `Pro`) and check what was actually rendered:

- **Mobile viewport & layout:** 390x844 mobile device emulation with touch (`playwright.config.ts`), intact card borders, zero horizontal overflow, no clipped text or overlapping elements, and primary actions within thumb reach.
- **Touch targets:** every interactive control is at least 44px tall and wide.
- **Contrast & hierarchy:** legible contrast ratios across text, badges, form controls and status states.
- **Copy & localization:** consistent language, regional form of address, accents, and singular/plural agreement; no raw translation keys, leaked placeholders, or untranslated strings.

<!-- kit:adapt: Write any additional project-specific visual and copy review rules for this project: the device context, brand or layout constraints, and specific localization conventions. One bullet each. -->

### 4. Report (Mandatory Screenshot Attachments)

Give {{OWNER}} a verification summary (**{{PERSONA_NAME_VERIFIER}}** format in `.agents/personas/verifier.md`):

- The check table as printed (`db`, `setup`, `build`, `boot`, `e2e`).
- Each acceptance criterion and the Playwright assertion + screenshot that proves it.
- Visual findings from the screenshots, with every cited screenshot attached or embedded.
- What still needs a human on a real device (haptics, native app handoffs, real network or sunlight conditions).

**Screenshot attachment rule (strictly enforced):**
- **Never post a PR verification comment or chat report that lists bare screenshot filenames** (for example `- Home (01-home.png): Mobile viewport...`) without uploading or embedding the rendered images.
- When posting a verification report to a GitHub PR with `gh pr comment` (requires GitHub CLI >= v2.99.0), upload every screenshot using `--attach "<path>#<alt>"` paired with a matching markdown image tag `![<alt>](<path>)` in `--body` (or `--body-file`). GitHub CLI v2.99.0+ automatically uploads each attached file to GitHub storage and rewrites the local markdown image path to a permanent GitHub asset URL:
<!-- kit:if module.openPr -->
  ```bash
  GH_TOKEN=$(gh auth token --user {{GH_ACCOUNT}}) gh pr comment <PR> --repo {{GH_REPO}} \
    --body "### Visual Review ({{PERSONA_NAME_VERIFIER}})\n\n- **Home**: ![Home](path/to/01-home.png)\n- **Login**: ![Login](path/to/02-login.png)" \
    --attach "path/to/01-home.png#Home screen at 390x844" \
    --attach "path/to/02-login.png#Login screen at 390x844"
  ```
<!-- kit:end -->
<!-- kit:if !module.openPr -->
  ```bash
  gh pr comment <PR> --repo <repo> \
    --body "### Visual Review ({{PERSONA_NAME_VERIFIER}})\n\n- **Home**: ![Home](path/to/01-home.png)\n- **Login**: ![Login](path/to/02-login.png)" \
    --attach "path/to/01-home.png#Home screen at 390x844" \
    --attach "path/to/02-login.png#Login screen at 390x844"
  ```
<!-- kit:end -->
- When reporting in chat, embed the rendered images directly (`![<alt>](/absolute/path/to/01-home.png)`) rather than listing bare filenames.

On a failure, quote the failing check and the log lines that matter, not the whole log.

## The config

`e2e.json` was written when the kit installed this skill. Change it in a normal PR when the build or boot changes. Besides the keys it shares with smoke-local (`dockerfile`, `appPort`, `healthPath`, `database`, `secretEnv`, `localUrlEnv`, `buildArgUrl`, `extraEnv`, `containerMigrate`):

- `mode`: `host` or `docker`, the default way to serve the app.
- `setup` and `build`: host commands, one line each, no shell syntax.
- `start`: the one host command that serves the built app; `startPortArgs` puts the port on its command line when it ignores `PORT` (for example `["--port"]`).
- `test`: the command that runs the suite.

## Rules

- Never pass a real secret or a production database URL to the script, and never put one in the config.
- Never commit screenshots or traces. The artifact folder lives outside the repo, and the script refuses one inside it.
- The unit test command stays fast; E2E specs live apart from unit tests and run only here or in CI.
